{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the given graph.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(graph with a constant speed of 20 meters per second)\n</p><p>The number of seconds required for a vehicle to travel a total distance of 100 m is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1744d0cc2b1278620af0c11dd8f6590581477f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2.5 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Through the graph, we can notice that the speed is constant.\n</p><p>This means that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf0c73361e30650e56eec75b6615b8f97896cfc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$st = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> represents the speed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> represents the time, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> represents the distance.\n</p><p>From the graph and problem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92d65beb32a3094fea8620dc9f79830e4b01346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 20 \\frac{m}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"34\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff821be704e8fa81cdf57ab60a1d8fa96958ff41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> m, giving:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d62e0e50fa9fe73679193bb5c348c6c1176eeb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20t = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Solving for t, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bc2ef78516fb01003693c823d005e12e9c756f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> s\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40308279e8c8d21b12a9fc83bb9b5a97f6537fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf { (E) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"201